   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Channel Recording**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **bit recording**: back after 104 archived shows (721 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **I Like Train Songs**: rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **Seven Weeks in County 1**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Love Among The Tombstones 2**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **St. James Hospital**: back after 62 archived shows (520 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **Debra’s Waltz**: rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **Remember To Cry**: rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2026-09-19.4channel** (recommended): source not stated; 25 songs; 154 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Super Mario Brothers \"Flagpole sound effect\" and \"Underground Theme\" (Koji Kondo) teases during Jarrod Walker chant [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2026-09-19.4channel**: taped by discocape; transferred by discocape; source: km184 + mk21 [1]. Also: Taped, tracked and transferred by discocape, using two mic pairs run through a Mix Pre 6 II at 32-bit/48kHz; Source 1 used Neumann KM184 mics in ORTF through GAK cables; Source 2 used Schoeps CMC1K/MK21 in wide ORTF [1]",
